{"phase": "request_done", "request_result": {"token_ids": [1206, 41020, 279, 18356, 421, 6681, 1330, 314, 279, 2250, 14336, 19715, 599, 279, 1788, 1829, 11, 567, 1902, 1118, 5517, 279, 2702, 1324, 314, 3102, 18957, 321, 1179, 1698, 279, 35531, 18957, 1332, 279, 1829, 7731, 369, 314, 279, 1304, 56014, 90, 17, 11, 220, 16, 11, 220, 15, 59, 30675, 318, 19186, 314, 799, 1829, 11, 799, 314, 2361, 11, 6942, 314, 279, 4688, 553, 271, 13962, 220, 16, 13, 10342, 5447, 314, 4230, 6371, 271, 760, 8697, 5435, 264, 2702, 314, 393, 20, 478, 220, 19, 478, 220, 18, 283, 220, 16, 17, 3, 19715, 13, 198, 1596, 513, 12945, 220, 18, 19715, 75150, 1973, 13329, 13, 8439, 279, 1906, 314, 12945, 1503, 524, 4766, 364, 279, 1534, 716, 314, 7736, 11, 567, 958, 26569, 310, 10724, 279, 2702, 1324, 314, 12103, 7062, 314, 220, 18, 19715, 421, 628, 381, 14336, 494, 279, 220, 16, 17, 13, 271, 13682, 198, 59, 1272, 90, 7354, 4230, 6371, 92, 283, 1088, 6649, 315, 90, 16, 17, 14728, 18, 92, 283, 1088, 35790, 90, 16, 17, 1088, 14695, 220, 16, 16, 1088, 14695, 220, 16, 15, 14728, 18, 1088, 14695, 220, 17, 1088, 14695, 220, 16, 92, 283, 220, 17, 1088, 14695, 220, 16, 16, 1088, 14695, 220, 16, 15, 283, 220, 17, 17, 15, 198, 13682, 271, 4272, 11, 1017, 513, 2972, 17, 17, 15, 332, 17763, 4222, 26569, 314, 220, 18, 19715, 13, 271, 13962, 220, 17, 13, 4356, 286, 71279, 470, 4230, 6371, 271, 760, 2876, 328, 325, 31654, 1330, 599, 279, 1788], "text": "To derive the probability that exactly two of the three drawn balls have the same color, we must first establish the total number of possible outcomes and then count the favorable outcomes where the color distribution is of the form $\\{2, 1, 0\\}$ (two of one color, one of another, zero of the third).\n\n### 1. Total Number of Outcomes\n\nThe bag contains a total of $5 + 4 + 3 = 12$ balls.\nWe are drawing 3 balls uniformly without replacement. Since the order of drawing does not matter for the final set of colors, we use combinations to calculate the total number 