rd).\n\n### 1. Total Number of Outcomes\n\nThe bag contains a total of $5 + 4 + 3 = 12$ balls.\nWe are drawing 3 balls uniformly without replacement. Since the order of drawing does not matter for the final set of colors, we use combinations to calculate the total number of distinct sets of 3 balls that can be drawn from the 12.\n\n$$\n\\text{Total Outcomes} = \\binom{12}{3} = \\frac{12 \\times 11 \\times 10}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1} = 2 \\times 11 \\times 10 = 220\n$$\n\nSo, there are **220** equally likely combinations of 3 balls.\n\n### 2. Counting Favorable Outcomes\n\nThe condition \"exactly two have the same", "id": "math-1536-mtp-r0", "case_id": "math-1536", "method": "mtp", "warmup": false, "max_tokens": 256, "repeat": 7, "sample_repeat": 0, "eval_group_size": 32, "prompt_sha256": "a9445d95bf1c54c7402f463ea9a4bfa7788e003cb246f83014b02876d2106a8c", "prompt_token_ids": [248045, 846, 198, 760, 2614, 26388, 14246, 17593, 369, 3870, 1132, 13, 21134, 279, 41559, 1238, 424, 26, 635, 524, 59987, 466, 2880, 279, 17593, 13, 198, 27, 15547, 29, 198, 41089, 3150, 220, 15, 15, 15, 15, 25, 264, 11525, 3816, 2531, 12, 15, 15, 15, 15, 26, 424, 12076, 264, 25293, 9463, 1518, 58565, 279, 1622, 13, 1061, 3150, 369, 3870, 2193, 11, 524, 449, 7359, 13, 198, 41089, 3150, 220, 15, 15, 15, 16, 25, 264, 11525, 3816, 2531, 12, 15, 15, 15, 16, 26, 424, 12076, 264, 25293, 9463, 1518, 58565, 279, 1622, 13, 1061, 3150, 369, 3870, 2193, 11, 524, 449, 7359, 13, 198, 41089, 3150, 220, 15, 15, 15, 17, 25, 264, 11525, 3816, 2531, 12, 15, 15, 15, 17, 26, 424, 12076, 264, 25293, 9463, 1518, 58565, 279, 1622, 13, 1061, 3150, 369, 3870, 2193, 11, 524, 449, 7359, 13, 198, 41089, 3150, 220, 15, 15, 15, 18, 25, 264, 11525, 3816, 2531, 12, 15, 15, 15, 18, 26, 424, 12076, 264, 25293, 9463, 1518, 58565, 279, 1622, 13, 1061, 3150, 369, 3870, 2193, 11, 524, 449, 7359, 13, 198, 41089, 3150, 220, 15, 15, 15, 19, 25, 264, 11525, 3816, 2531, 12, 15, 15, 15, 19, 26, 424, 12076, 264, 25293, 9463, 1518, 58565, 27